      "Explanation": "Luzu faces the wall names a recurrent case-action: when a visitor came, Luzu turned and faced the wall. Later masters repeatedly ask for its intent, answer with unrelated-looking phrases, reject proposed explanations, and compose verses under the case title. Later questioners repeatedly ask ‘what is the intent of Luzu facing the wall?’ Zifu Rubao answers that it has no connection; Huilin Hongji asks what there is to explain; Zhu'an Shigui answers with the five phases and celestial bodies. Verse collections preserve “Luzu faces the wall” as a case heading, while a later appraisal gives Luzu and Mazu's closed door twenty blows. These are public re-raisings of one remembered action, not descriptions of private contemplation."
    }
